SUMMARY:Art & Archives: Government of Ontario Art Collection + Archives To
 ur ($10)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\n**PLEASE read everything** over FIRST.
 \n\nNote--**the start time at 1pm**. Every few months\, we're able to add 
 a daytime/weekday important cultural destination.\n\n*$10 per person when 
 you RSVP on Meetup.*\n\nThis ART Crawl is on a *FRIDAY afternoon*--at **Yo
 rk University.**\n\nThis will be a very special and unique opportunity for
  us!\n\nWe'll visit/have tours at three locations: Ontario Archives/Ontari
 o Provincial Art Collection and The Goldfarb Gallery--which is--York Unive
 rsity public art gallery.\n\nThis is where the *Province of Ontario Art Co
 llection* is held--at the **Ontario Archives.**\n\nhttps://www.archives.go
 v.on.ca/art-collection/\n\nhttps://thegoldfarbgallery.ca/\n\nWe'll have a 
 private tour with the both Curator's (behind the scenes)\n\n(We've recentl
 y toured the City of Toronto Archives and the Government of Canada Archive
 s)\n\n**$10 per person.**\n\nEmailed to me directly in advance--**when you
  RSVP on Meetup**\n\n**Sent by E-transfer here:**\n\ntorontoisculture@gmai
 l.com\n\n***To confirm:***\nWe are visiting/touring TWO locations at York 
 University.\n\n1. Ontario Archives ( & **Province of Ontario Art Collectio
 n**)\n2. **Goldfarb Gallery** (this is York University's public gallery (o
 pened recently))\n\nBoth locations are a 5-10 mins WALK from York Universi
 ty TTC station.\nDirections and more details--\n\n[https://www.archives.go
 v.on.ca/hours-and-location/](https://www.archives.gov.on.ca/hours-and-loca
 tion/)\n\n(As this is a government office--they are open M/F from 9am-5pm 
 only)\n\nNo refunds/credit or cancellations. The TOUR is firmly booked.\n\
 nPlAN ahead--how will you get there? Transit? Drive? From St. George TTC--
 you'll arrive at the destination in about 30 minutes.
