SUMMARY:TPL Appel Salon Author Talk:  Edgar Allan Poe's Life & Work
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\n{ This event is now SOLD-OUT }\n\nMany
  of you are aware of the ongoing AUTHOR talks at TPL Reference Library. FR
 EE\n\nPls reserve your own ticket at the LINK below.\n\n\\*\\*Professor Em
 ily Ogden shares her intimate inquiry into the shadowy life and compelling
  work of the definitive author of the macabre.\n\nhttps://www.nytimes.com/
 2026/09/27/books/review/darkness-becomes-bright-emily-ogden.html\n\n***Sin
 ce Edgar Allan Poe’s mysterious death in 1849\, his stories and poems ha
 ve captivated millions of readers around the world***. Nearly two centurie
 s later\, why do we continue to descend into the darkness of his imaginati
 on—and of the genres\, from horror to crime\, that he pioneered?\n\nIn D
 arkness Becomes Bright\, Ogden plumbs the darkness within Poe and enters i
 t alongside him. She interweaves stories from his mysterious and tragic li
 fe with those of his most famous readers and translators\, showing us how 
 Poe’s vision echoes across the generations\, allowing us to make peace w
 ith our own flawed humanity.\n\nEmily Ogden speaks with author and critic 
 Naben Ruthnum about the brief life and immortal art of Edgar Allan Poe.\n\
 nQ&A and book signing to follow. Books available for purchase.\n\n**RESERV
 E your own FREE entry ticket--**\n\nhttps://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/event
 s/6a85b6ff4c610f0038954f12\n\nhttps://www.eventbrite.ca/e/art-of-darkness-
 edgar-allan-poes-life-work-tickets-1997593925204?aff=oddtdtcreator
