SUMMARY:Rapp Lecture on Contemporary Art: Lotus L. Kang and Ebony L. Hayne
 s (Free)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\n*The Rapp Lecture on Contemporary Art 
 features distinguished international leaders in the contemporary art world
 \, including artists\, curators\, critics\, and scholars. The program was 
 established in 2009 in honour of Carol and Morton Rapp.*\n\n***PLEASE rese
 rve your own FREE ticket*** in advance at the AGO link below.\n\n**Join ar
 tist Lotus L. Kang and curator Ebony L. Haynes as they discuss Kang’s mu
 lti-disciplinary creative practice. They’ll explore how Kang uses unstab
 le and light-sensitive materials to consider the relationship between the 
 body and its environments\, and how Haynes’ groundbreaking work leading 
 New York’s 52 Walker Gallery led to them working together.**\n\nLotus Ka
 ng is also short-listed for the upcoming Sobey Art Award. We'll visit her 
 works at the National Gallery in Ottawa--on our upcoming trip.\n\nhttps://
 www.gallery.ca/whats-on/sobey-art-award\n\n**Lotus L. Kang** is a New York
 -based artist whose practice spans sculpture\, photography\, and site-resp
 onsive installation. Recent solo exhibitions include the Bvlgari Pavilion 
 at the 61st Venice Biennale\, Frye Art Museum\, 52 Walker\, and Chisenhale
  Gallery. Her work has also been featured in the Whitney Biennial\, Shangh
 ai Biennial\, and New Museum Triennial\, and is held in major museum colle
 ctions including the Art Gallery of Ontario\, Stedelijk Museum\, Whitney M
 useum of American Art\, The Guggenheim Museum\, and Museum of Modern Art\,
  New York.\n\n3 mins intro..\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NK00tdA5Qa
 s\n\n**Ebony L. Haynes** is a New York-based curator and is the Global Hea
 d of Curatorial Projects at David Zwirner. She previously led the gallery
 ’s 52 Walker space in Tribeca\, NY. Haynes sits on the boards of Artists
  Space (New York)\, Topical Cream\, and the New Art Dealers Alliance. She 
 also runs Black Art Sessions: an online school that offers free profession
 al practice classes to Black students worldwide.\n\n**Reserve your own FRE
 E ticket here:**\n\nhttps://ago.ca/events/rapp-lecture-contemporary-art-lo
 tus-l.-kang-and-ebony-l.-haynes\n\nNote--this ticket gets you into the AGO
  (for FREE) from 6pm onwards.
